S("dGGMbqe4QYQ","How to climax in electronic music",
 "climax-break-structures-committed-turnaround-linear-rise-trilogy-fall-rise-hang-double-trilogy-insert-time-last",
 "Four climax/break structures for 8-bar phrased tracks: (1) committed turnaround, where the last part of an 8-bar loop is cut and deconstructed before the next section restarts; (2) linear rise, an 8-bar section with most elements removed that only builds (filters open, decay/release and reverb/delay times lengthen, new layers enter) until the full section returns; (3) trilogy break: fall (strip chords/rhythm to a few disorienting elements, optionally introduce a new chord progression), rise (percussion and opening filters build), hang (withhold the expected return for a bar with one unique phrase, then return); (4) double trilogy, where a long fall/rise is followed by a short fall/rise inside the same break",
 "Give ambient/cinematic and electronic tracks deliberate build/breakdown shapes. Delta vs arrangement-loop-to-song cluster (8-bar build template, breakdown after a drop, rule of three, no-riser transitions): a named vocabulary of four break shapes with an energy curve for each, the 'hang' withholding trick, and the rule to insert hang time last so the grid stays intact while arranging.",
 ["A DAW arrangement with an 8-bar-phrased loop or a finished main section","Filter, reverb and delay automation lanes"],
 [("main_section","arrangement","The full section the break leads back into",True),("phrase_bars","number","Phrase length, usually 8 bars",False),("hang_element","audio/midi","One unique phrase (pad swell, single chord, vocal or melodic line) for the hang",False)],
 [("break_section","arrangement","A turnaround, linear rise, trilogy or double-trilogy break with drawn automation"),("energy_map","text","Bar-by-bar energy curve (down/up) for the break")],
 ["Ambient adaptation: build tension with filter opening, longer reverb/delay and added sustained layers, not snare rolls, rapid stutters or clicky fills (Matt's preference).","Risers stay steady in pitch: use noise/filter sweeps or layered sustained notes, not pitch-glide risers.",EARLY,"Insert hang time last (insert-time command), after the rest of the arrangement is done, because it shifts everything after it off the bar grid.",ABL,"Portable module mapping: section = clip/scene/pattern; rise = filter cutoff + reverb send + layer gain ramps; works in any DAW, a tracker or a Web Audio scheduler."],
 [("Phrase the track in 8-bar loops and mark section boundaries.","Arrangement markers","8-bar grid visible"),
  ("Committed turnaround: at the end of an 8-bar loop, cut the last bar or two of the loop and deconstruct it (drop elements, filter or reverb-throw what remains), then restart the next section; swap a couple of elements in or out at that point.","Clip edit + automation","A section ending that commits to tension instead of a one-hit variation"),
  ("Linear rise: take an 8-bar section, remove most elements, then from the moment of removal build continuously: open low-pass filters, lengthen decay/release, raise reverb/delay time and send, and bring in new sustained layers or a noise sweep, so energy releases when the full section returns.","Filter/reverb/gain automation","One-direction build like drawing a bow"),
  ("Trilogy break, chapter 1 (fall): coming out of a full section, remove chords and most rhythm, leaving a few elements; hold 4-8 bars. Optionally introduce a new chord progression here, kept low in energy.","Mute/automation","Sparse, contemplative space"),
  ("Chapter 2 (rise): 4-8 bars of building: percussion returns, filters open, sustained layers and noise sweeps enter.","Automation","Listener expects the return"),
  ("Chapter 3 (hang): where the full section would return, withhold it for about a bar with one unique element (a single pad swell, chord or phrase), then bring the full section back.","Single element","Brief suspended moment before the release"),
  ("Double trilogy: inside one break, do a long fall + rise, then where the return is expected do a second, shorter fall + rise before the section comes back (filters can bring percussion back in).","Arrangement","Down-up-down-up energy curve"),
  ("When the arrangement is otherwise finished, insert the hang bar(s) with insert-time so everything after shifts together.","Insert time","Grid stays intact until the last step")],
 ["Each break shape has a written down/up energy curve and the automation follows it.","Rises use filter/reverb/layer automation only; no snare rolls or pitch-glide risers.","The hang is inserted last and the following section starts on its own downbeat."],
 ["arrangement","structure","breakdown","build","transition","climax","ambient","cinematic"])

S("Cx8mEhPdtB4","Make Ambient Like LOSCIL: Field Recordings to Floating Pads",
 "envelope-matched-chord-spacing-6s-attack-filter-env-long-verb-tail-synth-note-gated-field-recording-fx-4bar-lfo-sub",
 "Minimal Loscil-style ambient: a detuned saw pad with ~6.5 s attack and decay, low sustain, long release and a second long envelope opening the low-pass, playing chords spaced about 8-9 bars apart so the envelope and a long (~29 s) echo-reverb carry each chord into the next; a field recording routed into a synth's audio input (sidechain) so held MIDI notes gate it through the synth's filters and effects; a sparse release-tailed sine sequence into a dark reverb; and a unison saw sub on a 24 dB low-pass at 80-200 Hz with a free-running 4-bar LFO on cutoff",
 "Build a four-layer minimal ambient bed where timing and space do the work. Delta vs generative drone cluster (looper drone clips, follow-action pools) and arrangement-ambient: the chord loop length is set by the pad envelope (spacing = envelope + reverb tail), and field recordings are processed by playing a synth as a note gate, not by a sampler.",
 ["A synth with two envelopes and unison; a synth or effect that accepts sidechain/external audio (or a gate + filter chain)","A long echo/reverb (20 s+ decay)","A field recording loop"],
 [("key","string","e.g. D minor",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Slow, ~80-85",False),("field_recording","audio","Water/riverbed or similar loop",True)],
 [("pad_chords","midi+audio","Chords spaced so each tail reaches the next"),("texture","audio","Note-gated, filtered field recording"),("sine_sequence","midi","Fixed sparse sine line"),("sub","audio","Slowly filtered unison sub")],
 ["Steady pitch: the source randomised step-sequencer patterns and modulated tuning with a random LFO; here the sine sequence is a fixed hand-written pattern and all LFOs are smooth, periodic and on filter/volume only (Matt's preference).","No rapid clicking: keep the field recording's gate opening slow (attack >= 200 ms) and avoid crackly bubble-wrap-type sources.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: pad = saw osc + amp env + filter env; note-gated texture = audio in -> VCA keyed by MIDI gate -> filter -> delay/reverb; sub = saw unison -> LP24 with a 4-bar LFO."],
 [("Pad: saw with 3-4 unison voices, low detune; amp attack ~6.5 s, decay about the same, low sustain, long release; low-pass engaged with cutoff low.","Synth amp env + unison","Chords swell in slowly"),
  ("Add a second long envelope to the filter cutoff so each chord opens and closes the filter over its length.","Mod envelope -> cutoff","Long breathing filter per chord"),
  ("Write chords in key (e.g. C-F-G plus a high D in D minor); stagger note starts slightly by hand. Set the clip loop so the gap between chords matches the envelope length (8-9 bars at ~83 BPM), then shorten until each tail just meets the next chord.","MIDI clip loop length","Restrained chord rhythm, tails carry"),
  ("Put a long echo+reverb (~29 s decay) after the pad.","Reverb/delay","Wash connects the chords"),
  ("Texture: put a field recording on an audio track with its fader down (warped to loop length), route it as sidechain/external input into a synth's audio-input engine (or a gate keyed from MIDI), and hold one long MIDI note across the timeline so the synth gates it through.","Sidechain routing","Recording audible only through the synth"),
  ("Process the gated recording through the synth's filter, a multiband compressor, a ping-pong delay and a long reverb; add a slow smooth LFO on its volume and filter mix.","Synth FX + LFO","Washed, understated texture layer"),
  ("Sine sequence: sine with ~1.5 s decay, ~2 s release, low sustain; write a sparse fixed in-key pattern (D natural minor) and send it to a dark long reverb.","MIDI clip + reverb","Sparse bell-like line that blooms in the reverb"),
  ("Sub: the pad's root an octave or two down (e.g. D1) on a unison saw into a 24 dB low-pass at 80-200 Hz; free-running LFO on cutoff at 4 (or 8) bars; ~15% send to the same reverb; mix low.","Synth + LFO","Slowly moving foundation")],
 ["Each pad chord's tail reaches the next chord with no silent gap and no pile-up.","The field recording is silent when no MIDI note is held.","Sine line is identical on every loop pass (no random patterns)."],
 ["ambient","pad","field-recording","envelope","arrangement","minimal","sub","sine"])

S("LANPsnGB_yY","Made in Ableton Live: K. Hart on creative resampling, granular techniques and more",
 "arp-smear-pad-grain-delay-resample-stretch-2x-high-wet-echo-spectral-freeze-retrigger-16th-eq-band-plus-feedback-bandpass-loop-motion",
 "Arp-smear pad: arpeggiate a minor-9 chord (down pattern, long gate) through a grain delay and a delay with reverse, resample it, stretch the audio to double length with pitch-preserving warp, then smear it with a high-wet, high-feedback echo, a spectral freeze retriggered every 1/16 note and an EQ band-limit; plus a feedback-mode distortion on a melodic loop (100% feedback path, dotted 1/2 time, band-pass centred ~3 kHz with its width modulated by a 1-bar LFO) resampled and re-looped for a second melodic element",
 "Turn a simple arpeggio into a lush background pad, and a static loop into a moving melodic layer, by resampling. Delta vs granular cluster (live rolling-buffer granular, sample-to-synth keygroup, sampler loop chord pad): the source is an arpeggiated chord, smoothed into a pad by stretch + echo + retriggered spectral freeze, not a granular cloud from a sample.",
 ["A synth and arpeggiator, a grain delay, a delay, an echo with feedback, a spectral freeze/time effect (or a freeze reverb), an EQ","A distortion or delay with a filtered feedback path"],
 [("chord","midi","e.g. A minor 9",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Track tempo",True),("loop","audio","Optional melodic loop for the feedback layer",False)],
 [("arp_smear_pad","audio","Resampled, stretched, frozen pad clip"),("feedback_loop_layer","audio","Resampled feedback-band-pass melodic clip")],
 ["Steady pitch: grain delay pitch and pitch-randomness at 0, warp mode must preserve pitch when stretching; the source's random MIDI generator, random hat velocity, random panning and 255 ms bass glide are dropped (Matt's preference).","Spectral freeze retrigger at 1/16 must sound smooth (crossfaded), not like a clicking stutter; if it clicks, retrigger every 1/4 or 1/2 bar instead.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: arp -> grain/granular delay -> resample -> time-stretch x2 -> feedback delay -> freeze buffer retriggered on a clock -> band EQ; feedback layer = delay line with band-pass in the loop, LFO on its Q."],
 [("Write a one-chord MIDI clip (A minor 9) into a soft synth; arpeggiator on, down pattern, rate as wanted, a few octave steps, long gate.","Arpeggiator","Flowing arpeggio"),
  ("Add a grain delay (pitch 0) and a delay with reverse repeats after the synth.","Grain delay + delay","Textured, broken-up repeats"),
  ("Resample to a new audio track while adjusting grain-delay spray/frequency by hand.","Resampling","Raw textured audio clip"),
  ("Warp the clip (pitch-preserving mode) and stretch it to double length.","Warp stretch","Slower, same pitch"),
  ("Add an echo with high dry/wet and raised feedback so notes smear together.","Echo","No single note stands out"),
  ("Add a spectral freeze with freeze on and retrigger every 1/16 note to smooth the sound into a sustained pad; then an EQ to confine it to its frequency band.","Spectral time + EQ","Lush pad sitting behind the track"),
  ("Feedback layer: on a melodic loop, a distortion in feedback routing with 100% blend to the feedback path, feedback amount up, time set to dotted 1/2, feedback band-pass centred ~3 kHz; modulate band-pass width with a 1-bar synced LFO; add light distortion.","Feedback distortion + LFO","Loop gains movement and harmonics"),
  ("Resample it, then loop short regions of the recording (e.g. bars 18-22) and move the start point to find new phrases.","Audio clip loop","Second melodic element derived from the loop")],
 ["Pad clip has no audible individual arp attacks after the smear chain.","Pitch of the stretched clip matches the original key.","Feedback layer's band-pass width changes once per bar."],
 ["pad","arpeggio","resampling","grain-delay","spectral-freeze","smear","feedback","loop"])

S("Pf0at7zMSDw","Unlock Punchy Bass in Serum | Mixing Trick for ANY DAW",
 "punchy-808-2nd-3rd-harmonic-partials-subtle-unipolar-coarse-pitch-dive-convex-decay-fm-ratio-half-transient-two-stage-softclip-zero-cross-print",
 "Punchy 808 from the source: start with a sine and set character with the 2nd and 3rd harmonic partials (additive/wavetable editor) before any distortion; add punch with a subtle envelope on coarse tune in unipolar mode so the dive ends exactly on the note; design in the key where it sounds best (not forced to C); shape the decay curve (concave = kick-like and dynamic, convex = long sustained 808); add filter drive or tube warp, an FM-from-sine layer at ratio 0.5 (bubbly) or higher (metallic) with its own short envelope for a transient, two soft clippers in series and a limiter; print it and trim/fade to a zero crossing",
 "Make a punchy, controllable 808/sub one-shot. Delta vs bass cluster (four bass types incl. punchy 808 with 35 ms pitch punch, interval-aware low end, short kick + ducked subs): harmonic-partial voicing as the main character control, a unipolar endpoint-targeted pitch dive, decay-curve shape as a punch control, and an FM-ratio transient instead of a pitch dive.",
 ["A synth with editable partials or a harmonic wavetable editor, mod envelopes with curve control and FM between oscillators","Soft clipper, limiter, sample editor"],
 [("key_note","string","Root note the 808 will be designed and printed on",True),("style","enum","kick-like (concave) or long (convex)",False)],
 [("bass_808","audio","Printed one-shot with zero-crossing start/end"),("patch","preset","Source patch for re-printing in other keys")],
 ["Steady pitch: the coarse-tune dive is a short transient (tens of ms) in unipolar mode ending exactly on the note, never a wobble or slide; the source's pogo/ping-pong pitch modes and long pitch bends are left out (Matt's preference).","Keep the FM transient soft and low-ratio; avoid metallic clicky ratios on ambient tracks.","Check level after each saturation stage; stay below clipping before printing.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: sine + partials 2/3 = additive or 3-sine stack; pitch env -> coarse tune; FM osc ratio 0.5 with AD env; soft clip x2 -> limiter."],
 [("Initialise a patch to a sine; play the bass line an octave down.","Synth","Plain sine sub"),
  ("Open the harmonic/partials editor and raise or lower the 2nd and 3rd harmonics until the 808 has the wanted character (bubbly vs round).","Partials editor","Character set at the source, no distortion yet"),
  ("Assign a mod envelope (sustain 0, short decay) to coarse tune, with a gentle curve and small amount; set the routing unipolar so the dive ends exactly on the played note.","Mod env -> coarse tune","Punch without pitch drifting below the note"),
  ("Pick the key where the 808 sounds best and design there, then print in that key.","Keyboard","Best-sounding fundamental"),
  ("Shape the amp decay curve: concave for a dynamic kick-like 808, convex for a long sustained one; adjust sustain curve so the tail rings out naturally.","Amp env curves","Punch vs length set by curve"),
  ("Add saturation: filter drive or a tube warp/distortion mode (one stage at a time), matching level when comparing.","Filter drive / tube","Rounded harmonics, more perceived punch"),
  ("Optional transient: enable an FM-from-sine source at ratio 0.5 (lower = bubbly, higher = metallic) with its own short envelope on FM amount, then low-pass to tame highs.","FM + envelope","Short punch that isn't a pitch dive"),
  ("Chain two soft clippers (post-gain of the first drives the second), a light EQ and a limiter with saturation off to square off the peak.","Soft clip x2 + limiter","Dense, controlled 808"),
  ("Print/record it, fade out the tail, and set any loop or edit points on zero crossings so it doesn't click; save at 32-bit stereo.","Sample editor","Clean one-shot ready for a sampler")],
 ["Pitch dive ends on the played note (tuner reads the root after the transient).","Printed sample starts and ends on zero crossings with no click.","A/B at matched level shows the partials change, not just loudness, makes the character difference."],
 ["bass","808","punch","harmonics","pitch-envelope","fm","soft-clip","sub"])

S("Aqe3ISng8jA","How To Make Pads From Noise/Recordings Like Burial | Inspired By...",
 "noise-recording-tuned-to-key-stacked-max-q-eq-boosts-at-root-freeze-flatten-chromatic-sampler-pad-attack-verb-delay-sidechain-eq-automation",
 "Key-tuned noise pad: blend two recordings (one with voices/ambience, one with harsh white-noise content), bounce them, then boost a single very narrow (max-Q) EQ band at the key's root frequency (e.g. 440 Hz for A) to full gain and duplicate that EQ 3-5 times until a sine-like tone emerges; freeze/flatten (bounce in place), load into a sampler with the root note set to that pitch, play chords so the noise is in key, add filter attack, reverb and delay, light sidechain ducking to the beat, and automate EQ over the arrangement to bring more or less noise in",
 "Get synth-free air and texture pads that sit in key. Delta vs brightness cluster (synth-native noise-osc air, tape-noise bed, tuned noise layers on drums) and generative drones (pitch-locked noise layers): resonance is imposed on any recording by stacked narrow EQ boosts at the key's root, then the printed result is played chromatically as a sampler pad.",
 ["Two noisy field recordings or noise samples","Parametric EQ with high Q, a sampler, reverb, delay, compressor with sidechain"],
 [("recordings","audio","Two noise/ambience recordings (voices, beach, traffic, hiss)",True),("key_root_hz","number","Root frequency, e.g. 440 for A, 220/110 for lower",True),("chords","midi","Chord progression in that key",True)],
 [("tuned_noise_pad","audio/sampler","In-key noise pad playable from MIDI"),("eq_automation","automation","Arrangement lanes bringing noise in/out")],
 ["Steady pitch: the source's advanced level ramped the sampler's loop start with a fast 30 Hz LFO, giving random scrubbing and a ramped pitch effect; it is dropped. Keep the sample start fixed and loop with a crossfade (Matt's preference).","No rapid clicking: very short loop lengths buzz/click, so loop at least a few hundred ms with a crossfade.","Protect ears: stacked max-gain EQs can ring loudly; lower the track fader before adding each copy and limit the output.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: noise source -> 3-5 series peaking EQs (max Q, max gain at root Hz) -> bounce -> sampler (root = that note) -> amp env -> reverb/delay -> sidechain comp."],
 [("Blend sections of two recordings (one with voices/ambience, one with harsh noise), bounce to one clip and raise gain.","Audio edit + bounce","One noisy source clip"),
  ("Add an EQ band at the key root (e.g. 440 Hz for A) at maximum Q and maximum gain, with the fader down first.","Parametric EQ","A faint sine-like tone appears"),
  ("Duplicate that EQ until the pitch is clearly audible (3 copies, up to ~5 for quiet sources).","Series EQs","Noise now has a clear key centre"),
  ("Freeze and flatten (bounce in place) the result.","Bounce","Printed tuned-noise clip"),
  ("Load it into a sampler with the root note set to the tuned pitch (A); play chords from MIDI. Speech becomes unintelligible because each key plays at a different rate.","Sampler","In-key noise chords"),
  ("Lengthen the amp/filter attack so chords swell, then add reverb and delay to blur leftover details.","Envelope + FX","Soft, washed pad"),
  ("Set the sample start a little in and loop a section with a crossfade so every note doesn't begin on the same recognisable spot.","Sampler loop + crossfade","Smooth sustain without a repeated head"),
  ("Add a compressor sidechained to the beat (fast attack, eased release) so the pad ducks; automate the EQ over the arrangement (low-passed in some sections, more noise in others).","Sidechain comp + EQ automation","Organic, in-key texture that breathes with the arrangement")],
 ["A tuner on the printed clip shows a stable root at the chosen note.","Chords played from MIDI are audibly in key with the track.","No clicks at loop points."],
 ["noise","air","field-recording","pad","sampler","eq","brightness","texture"])
